WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.036
A 100-dollar watch

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:04.276
can be 99.99 percent

00:00:04.088 --> 00:00:04.795
accurate

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.525
Mechanical watches

00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:07.315
have kept time

00:00:07.126 --> 00:00:08.683
for 500 years

00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:09.968
and this interactive

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.336
3D page explains

00:00:11.148 --> 00:00:12.043
how a modern

00:00:11.855 --> 00:00:12.727
one works

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.224
The author calls

00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:15.062
it fascinating that

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:16.017
a well-calibrated

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.668
purely mechanical device

00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:18.411
can keep time

00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:20.486
with 99.99 percent

00:00:20.298 --> 00:00:22.373
accuracy for 100 dollars

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.759
The gear math

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.313
checks out

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.327
the third wheel

00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:26.247
runs 7 and

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:26.884
a half times

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:27.391
slower

00:00:27.603 --> 00:00:28.417
and the center

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.207
wheel 8 times

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:30.020
slower than that

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.259
so 7 and

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:31.907
a half times

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:32.733
8 is 60

00:00:32.863 --> 00:00:33.723
and the center

00:00:33.535 --> 00:00:34.478
wheel turns once

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:34.985
an hour

00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:36.540
Full story on

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:37.247
the dashboard
